WEBVTT

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:45.410
<i>Kanjizai bosatsu. Gyou jin hannya haramitta ji.</i>
<i>Shooken goon kaikuu. Do issai kuyaku.</i>

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:52.290
<i>Sharishi. Shiki fu i kuu. Kuu fu ishiki.</i>
<i>Shiki soku ze kuu. Kuu soku--</i>

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:59.950
Ritsuko, I'm going to work.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.000
"Dream Space of Bread and Curry VOYAGER"
What... the... Kerner!

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.160
What... the... Kerner!

00:02:35.160 --> 00:02:36.410
"Kerner variety. A white grape that's made
by crossing Trollinger and Riesling."
What... the... Kerner!

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:38.000
"No matter the quality of soil, it is resistant
to frost. In Japan, it is grown in Hokkaido."
What... the... Kerner!

00:02:38.580 --> 00:02:42.750
"Episode 3: You All Are Soft"
What are you screaming about? I told
you we're letting you go after the summer festival.

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.200
Didn't you listen to the radio?
I did my best to promote this place!

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:48.410
You did your best, huh?

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:52.410
It was only three seconds long and it was
for the food stall, not this restaurant!

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:56.410
I could care less about that stall.
Advertising it was a waste.

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.580
I never said we'd keep you if you
promoted us on the radio anyway.

00:02:59.580 --> 00:03:01.790
Okay, fine! I got it!

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:03.830
I'll be this restaurant's soldier for hire.

00:03:03.830 --> 00:03:05.160
"Soldier for hire?"
You mean, a security guard?

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:09.700
I'll stay here every night for maximum security.
I'll put together the family meal myself.

00:03:09.700 --> 00:03:13.040
The world isn't all rainbows and candy, my dear.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:15.700
You need to grow up!

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:22.830
Miss Koda, it's not like you were a bad worker.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:27.450
You never messed up the orders
and got along with the customers.

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.080
But to achieve my "dream space" vision,

00:03:29.080 --> 00:03:33.580
I need a worker who can do more
than just get along with the customers.

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:39.370
A "dream space"? Please! He's got no compassion!

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:43.830
See, what did I tell you? Not even
a parting gift. He's so cheap!

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.660
It's a tough world we live in.

00:03:47.750 --> 00:03:50.040
It's always been a mystery to me.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.250
But don't you think Mr. Takarada's
always been rude to you, Miss Minare?

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:58.040
Didn't you know? He's gay.
He's the handsy type, too.

00:03:58.040 --> 00:03:59.750
What? Really?

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:03.160
Haven't you looked at the pictures of
celebrities that ate there on that wall

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.950
between the kitchen and dining room?

00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:06.700
It's obvious when you look at that.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:08.910
What? Um...

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:13.620
Whenever he's posing with a lady,
he seems normal and all...

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.250
But when it's a young guy,
he has his arm around their butt.

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:20.540
What? Whoa! You're right!

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:24.500
No wonder! That explains why he keeps
touching my butt in the kitchen!

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.120
What? Are you serious?

00:04:26.120 --> 00:04:30.250
I can't believe you didn't realize it until now.

00:04:30.250 --> 00:04:35.290
Starting tomorrow it's just you two men,
a dream space of roses!

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:37.830
Enjoy your turmeric-colored sausage curry.

00:04:37.830 --> 00:04:39.500
Please stop!

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:48.790
Shoot... I'm jobless now.
What am I going to do?

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.750
I don't want to go back to school...

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:54.410
I'm here to help. Let's look for jobs tomorrow.

00:04:54.410 --> 00:04:55.500
Why is this happening?

00:04:55.500 --> 00:05:00.750
To balance out my bad luck with men,
I should have great luck with my career!

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.540
This isn't what was promised!

00:05:03.540 --> 00:05:05.540
Who promised you that?

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:07.910
The great master Ryuji Kagami,
of course! Dammit!

00:05:07.910 --> 00:05:08.950
"Your 2018 horoscope
Ryuji Kagami
Astrology A Gift From the Stars"

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:09.910
"Your 2018 horoscope
Ryuji Kagami
Astrology A Gift From the Stars"
From the women's magazine?

00:05:10.750 --> 00:05:15.870
I thought I could rely
on my savings for a while.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:19.700
But my lease is up and my car's due
for an inspection next month.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.370
Things are really bad for me right now.

00:05:27.290 --> 00:05:29.080
Want to stay at my place?

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:32.950
What...?

00:05:36.790 --> 00:05:38.950
Whoa! Are you okay?

00:05:38.950 --> 00:05:41.250
Whoa, that freaked me out.

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:45.580
I just did a quick simulation of what
it would be like if I lived with you.

00:05:45.580 --> 00:05:47.200
What happened...?

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:51.450
You ended up being stabbed in the stomach
and killed at Tanukikoji by some strange woman.

00:05:51.450 --> 00:05:54.500
What kind of world do you think I live in?

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:57.160
Yeah!

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:59.450
Phew. That's the foot stomp
technique to sober up.

00:05:59.450 --> 00:06:01.000
You practice <i>kenpo</i>?

00:06:01.000 --> 00:06:03.750
I just yelled and stomped my foot hard!

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.370
Don't take a drunk's word seriously, you idiot.

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:11.120
Nakahara... What brought us together...

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:14.620
...was soup curry, remember? So...

00:06:15.620 --> 00:06:18.870
I want to keep things round
and simple, like soup!

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:22.950
"Is that a gesture for a plate?"
Miss Minare, you're deflecting
my feelings with a silly metaphor...

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:27.040
I don't mind if there's no se--
Um... lover-like activities, really.

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:27.620
For a little bit.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:30.160
No, not possible. I sleep completely naked.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:33.790
Really? Me, too!
Sleeping in the nude feels the best!

00:06:33.790 --> 00:06:35.200
Idiot! I was testing you.

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.500
"*An extremely annoying situation"
I wear pajamas, thank you very much.

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:41.000
"*An extremely annoying situation"
That totally turned me off, by the way.

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:42.080
Listen, Nude Dude!

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.040
Uh, yes?

00:06:43.040 --> 00:06:46.080
Huh? You really want me to call you
"Nude Dude" from now on?

00:06:46.080 --> 00:06:48.540
Of course not. I just responded
without thinking.

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:51.750
"Zenra"
Then how about the Japanese word for nude,
"<i>zenra</i>," spelled with fancy characters?

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.040
"Zenra"
S-Sure...

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:55.080
"Zenra"
Better than "Nude Dude," that's for sure.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:07:00.080
Zenra! You and I, this is the last time we meet.
We'll part ways now.

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:05.660
However! If I really go broke, I'll most likely
appear in front of you again.

00:07:05.660 --> 00:07:07.250
Until then...

00:07:08.120 --> 00:07:11.370
Farewell!

00:07:11.370 --> 00:07:16.700
She makes a strong exit,
stating only what's convenient for her...

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:22.580
She expects me to help her
when she's desperate, pretty much.

00:07:22.580 --> 00:07:25.540
Where would you find a guy
who'd be happy with that?

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:27.250
Right here...

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.950
I got 250,000 yen in savings...

00:07:37.950 --> 00:07:42.950
I need to make a 60,000-yen deposit
by the end of the month...

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:46.870
The car inspection and lease renewal...
That's 200,000 yen.

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:51.790
What the hell is going to happen to me...

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:55.410
I want someone to let me stay with them...

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:58.950
Someone... Oh, Mitsuo...

00:07:58.950 --> 00:08:01.410
Die... seriously...

00:08:01.410 --> 00:08:04.870
I like the Kirin beer booth...

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:10.200
But the food at the World's
Beer Garden was the best...

00:08:10.200 --> 00:08:13.910
This is a dilemma...

00:08:13.910 --> 00:08:17.120
Ah... I gotta take a shower...

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:40.250
Sorry, would you mind? Your clothes...

00:08:40.250 --> 00:08:40.790
No!

00:08:40.790 --> 00:08:42.120
What?

00:08:48.910 --> 00:08:51.290
"Connected Call Time"
Yes, this is Sapporo Kita Police Station.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:53.000
Police Officer, there's an assaulter in my room!

00:08:53.000 --> 00:08:55.000
Well, I was the one who got violent, but...

00:08:55.000 --> 00:08:58.620
He's a flannel-shirt wearing dude
with center-parted hair!

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:07.120
So, if I'm understanding correctly,
what happened was...

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.330
"Not again..."
Every time I get drunk, I always
pass out on your doorstep.

00:09:12.330 --> 00:09:15.750
And you carry me up the stairs
on your back to my place.

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:18.660
After you put me down in my room,
you neatly place my shoes side-by-side.

00:09:18.660 --> 00:09:20.540
It was you the whole time!

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:23.160
I didn't really have a choice.

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:25.950
At first I tried bringing you outside,
but you kept coming back.

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:29.620
I tried locking you out, but you would
bawl and bang on my door.

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:33.040
You probably thought I was
your boyfriend or something.

00:09:35.160 --> 00:09:37.870
So... You're telling me...

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.620
Whenever I drink until I black out and go home,

00:09:41.620 --> 00:09:45.080
I'm not the organized type who places my shoes
neatly side-by-side before I go to bed...

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:50.120
I've always been the self-destructive type
who causes a public disturbance?!

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:54.160
Tone down that act as if you were
Keanu Reeves waking up in The Matrix.

00:09:54.160 --> 00:09:57.080
Could you please just go home?

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:57.450
--Oh... my... god...

00:09:57.450 --> 00:10:01.080
--So the case is closed.
We should get going, too.
--Oh... my... god...

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.370
Oh, yes. Thank you for your time.

00:10:14.120 --> 00:10:17.370
Um... Mr. Oki...?

00:10:17.370 --> 00:10:22.290
Any chance you'll be visiting your parents
in September and looking for a house-sitter?

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:23.830
No way.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:25.290
--Good evening, the time is 2 AM.
It's time for J-Hits Planet.

00:10:25.290 --> 00:10:26.370
--Huh?
--Good evening, the time is 2 AM.
It's time for J-Hits Planet.

00:10:26.370 --> 00:10:28.500
--Good evening, the time is 2 AM.
It's time for J-Hits Planet.

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:33.700
Hey, what's up? There's a broadcast
happening now, but I can talk.

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:38.080
Mr. Mato! This is code red!
Code red! I'll take the radio gig!

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:43.830
Yeah... That's right. And... arrange me
a place to sleep at Moiwayama Radio!

00:10:43.830 --> 00:10:45.700
The storage?! Come on...

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.450
--Today's first request is Sambomaster's
"Your Warmth is Calling For Me."

00:10:46.450 --> 00:10:50.200
--Sure, whatever. Storage it is!
--Today's first request is Sambomaster's
"Your Warmth is Calling For Me."

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:56.540
Thank you for letting me stay here!

00:10:56.540 --> 00:11:00.160
What, are you going to climb
Mt. Moiwa after this?

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.620
Why would I climb that thing
when I don't even have a boyfriend!

00:11:03.620 --> 00:11:06.750
I brought the things I need to make
the storage feel like home.

00:11:06.750 --> 00:11:08.660
"You know they sell the 'love padlock' to put
around the 'Bell of Happiness' at the summit!"
Ah, got it. Sorry.

00:11:09.000 --> 00:11:14.040
Before we set you up in storage,
let's talk business.

00:11:15.160 --> 00:11:19.330
Could I drop this off somewhere first?
It weighs over 20 kilograms.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:21.790
What did you bring besides
your clothes and futon?

00:11:21.790 --> 00:11:24.870
The paperback version of <i>Glass Mask</i>, of course.

00:11:24.870 --> 00:11:26.330
Please enjoy.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:28.040
Ah, thank you.

00:11:30.870 --> 00:11:32.750
Minare...

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:37.910
Would you be interested in hosting
a program with your name in the title?

00:11:37.910 --> 00:11:40.370
A program with my name in the title?

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:44.500
"Commemoration of Graduation
1985 INGRY MONGRY"
Oh, sorry. For some reason,
INGRY MONGRY popped into my head.

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:46.500
"Commemoration of Graduation
1985 INGRY MONGRY"
"Takes me back..."
Seriously, why?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:49.120
So, did I hear you right?

00:11:49.120 --> 00:11:55.080
You're really asking me if I'm interested
in doing a program with my name in the title?

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:57.620
Like <i>Tamori Club </i>and <i>Tetsuko's Room</i>?

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:01.830
Those are examples of TV shows. For radio,

00:12:01.830 --> 00:12:05.000
it'd be more like:
Minare Koda's All Night Nippon.

00:12:05.000 --> 00:12:05.750
"aiko, Masaharu Fukuyama, Chiharu Matsuyama,
Kohmi Hirose, Takeshi, Keisuke Kuwata,
Tsuyoshi Nagabuchi, Porno Graffiti"

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:07.660
"aiko, Masaharu Fukuyama, Chiharu Matsuyama,
Kohmi Hirose, Takeshi, Keisuke Kuwata,
Tsuyoshi Nagabuchi, Porno Graffiti"
All...

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:11.000
"Yumi Matsutoya, Ryuichi Kawamura,
INGRY MONGRY, Kobukuro,
Hikaru Ijuin, Shun Oguri"

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:13.450
Well, MRS isn't a major station,
so there's no way

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:18.830
it would become nearly as popular
as that long-running show.

00:12:18.830 --> 00:12:20.040
Thought so.

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:25.870
Anyway... Have you heard of our show,
Sound High Tide?

00:12:25.870 --> 00:12:26.870
Never.

00:12:26.870 --> 00:12:30.500
I see. It's one of our longest running shows.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:34.580
We're thinking of cutting it short
to get your program on air.

00:12:34.580 --> 00:12:38.330
What? So, will I have a segment
in that program or something?

00:12:38.330 --> 00:12:41.290
Just like what happened with
Miss Madoka Chishiro's program?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:42.910
No, not quite.

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:48.000
You'll round up your own sponsors
to produce your own program.

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:53.830
Minare, you once called MRS
just some local Sapporo radio station,

00:12:53.830 --> 00:12:56.410
but we're actually affiliated with JFL.

00:12:56.410 --> 00:12:59.450
JFL stands for Japan FM League.

00:12:59.450 --> 00:13:01.080
So what about it?

00:13:01.080 --> 00:13:03.870
We have seven relay stations
throughout Hokkaido.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:06.580
Your voice is going to be heard
all over Hokkaido.

00:13:06.580 --> 00:13:08.950
"Personification of a long-running show."

00:13:08.950 --> 00:13:12.160
"Personification of a long-running show."
But of course, it'll only be aired in Hokkaido

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.660
so don't expect to become
some big-name celebrity.

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.830
It's radio, after all.

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:18.910
No! Wait, wait a minute, Mr. Mato.

00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:21.450
I have no desire to become famous or anything...

00:13:21.450 --> 00:13:26.160
Liar. You were totally fantasizing
about a celebrity lifestyle.

00:13:26.160 --> 00:13:28.330
I'm content being the charming worker
at the curry shop.

00:13:28.330 --> 00:13:29.580
You were fired, weren't you?

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.500
Don't you judge me!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:35.160
You're mistaken if you think all women
dream of marrying celebrities.

00:13:35.160 --> 00:13:39.120
Oh, well, I don't know about all that...

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:44.500
Mr. Mato, what I'm most concerned about...

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:48.290
...is this.

00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:48.620
This?

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.500
Not the Yo-kai Medal!

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:55.200
What? You think I'm twelve or something?
Please don't try to change the subject.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.250
Minare...

00:14:02.250 --> 00:14:05.200
Unfortunately, the money's
going to depend on you.

00:14:05.200 --> 00:14:09.540
Radio ratings are calculated
differently than TV ratings.

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:12.000
They're calculated by individual surveys.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.290
Positive responses will get you a raise;

00:14:14.290 --> 00:14:17.540
negative responses will get you
canned by the sponsors.

00:14:17.540 --> 00:14:20.120
That's also true for TV.

00:14:20.120 --> 00:14:25.000
The reason why I'm giving you,
an amateur, this opportunity...

00:14:26.700 --> 00:14:30.500
...is because I'm confident that
you'll bring in high ratings.

00:14:30.500 --> 00:14:35.830
Pretty sure he just deflected
my question about the salary...

00:14:36.910 --> 00:14:40.200
I know I'm the one asking for the job...

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:46.700
But I'm still confused as to why you're
so convinced I'm suited for this, Mr. Mato.

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:49.120
Huh?

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:56.750
Is she... an actress or something?

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:59.040
Don't you think you look like her?

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.040
What?!

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:07.410
To be honest, one of the reasons
I'm convinced is that you kind of look like her.

00:15:07.410 --> 00:15:09.080
Is he hitting on me right now?

00:15:09.080 --> 00:15:10.040
"You're as beautiful"
Is he hitting on me right now?

00:15:10.040 --> 00:15:12.580
"You're as beautiful"
"as an actress..."
In some sense, yes.

00:15:12.580 --> 00:15:14.250
Oh...

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:18.040
So, before I ask you who she is,

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:22.330
what does me looking like her
have to do with the ratings?

00:15:22.330 --> 00:15:23.620
Listeners won't see my face.

00:15:23.620 --> 00:15:25.160
Nothing, really.

00:15:25.160 --> 00:15:26.330
Come on...

00:15:26.330 --> 00:15:28.290
Hey, old man...

00:15:28.290 --> 00:15:32.950
You think I'm dumb and always try to confuse me.
Like when you mentioned that comedian before...

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:34.450
Ah.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:36.790
Oh... Is she...?

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:40.950
That's right. She's the comedian, Sissel Komei.

00:15:40.950 --> 00:15:43.620
You don't just look like her...

00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:46.540
Your skills also resemble hers.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.040
We can talk more about that another day.

00:15:50.040 --> 00:15:57.200
But you'll most likely hear about her
from someone other than me.

00:15:57.200 --> 00:15:59.330
Huh?

00:15:59.330 --> 00:16:01.830
Okay, enough about her...

00:16:01.830 --> 00:16:05.200
So tell me more about the Sound High Tide thing.

00:16:05.200 --> 00:16:07.040
What day and time does it air?

00:16:07.040 --> 00:16:11.000
I don't expect to make
a living working in radio.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:14.080
I need to work in a part-time job, too.

00:16:14.080 --> 00:16:15.910
Huh?

00:16:15.910 --> 00:16:17.870
It's this time right here.

00:16:17.870 --> 00:16:21.910
It airs every day, just so you know...

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.040
Oh, when is it?

00:16:23.040 --> 00:16:24.750
It's this slot right here.

00:16:24.750 --> 00:16:26.200
"3:30 AM Sound High Tide"

00:16:26.290 --> 00:16:29.040
Oh... Uh, um...

00:16:29.040 --> 00:16:32.540
Now the question is, how do we find a sponsor?

00:16:32.540 --> 00:16:34.580
Old man, you gotta be kidding me!

00:16:34.580 --> 00:16:37.410
This isn't a program, it's more like
a radio transmission test show!

00:16:37.410 --> 00:16:42.660
With barely any listeners, what company's going
to want to sponsor a program at this time! Hey!

00:16:43.790 --> 00:16:46.620
Thanks for letting me stay with you.

00:16:46.620 --> 00:16:47.620
Huh?

00:16:47.620 --> 00:16:51.370
You should tilt that sideways when you come in.

00:16:53.330 --> 00:16:57.700
Your place is so organized... Strangely...

00:16:57.700 --> 00:17:00.500
Oh, you can put your stuff right over here.

00:17:00.500 --> 00:17:02.200
Well, let's cheers.

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:04.950
Yes, it's great to have you.

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:11.750
Sadly, even as your senior,
I can only afford discount wine.

00:17:11.750 --> 00:17:15.000
Two bottles of this Chablis was only
2,400 yen! Incredibly cheap!

00:17:15.000 --> 00:17:15.950
Thanks Jupiter!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:18.120
It's very delicious!

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:22.000
You really saved me, though.
That storage didn't have heat.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.080
There was no way I would've
survived until spring.

00:17:24.080 --> 00:17:26.410
She was planning on staying there until spring?

00:17:26.410 --> 00:17:31.200
Even if there was heat, we wouldn't
let anyone stay in the storage room.

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:34.370
Oh, Nanba, what's your first name?

00:17:34.370 --> 00:17:35.910
Oh, it's Mizuho.

00:17:35.910 --> 00:17:39.080
Mizuho, you're seriously a doll!

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:41.580
You must've been popular
with the boys as a student.

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.830
What was the freakiest present
you ever received?

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:48.700
Miss Minare, you're totally pretending
to be drunk right now, right?

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:49.830
"I wasn't that popular..."
Oh... Yeah... Sorry.

00:17:49.830 --> 00:17:51.910
Oh... Yeah... Sorry.

00:17:51.910 --> 00:17:53.290
Ah, thank you very much.

00:17:53.290 --> 00:17:55.410
So, what does a radio station
assistant director do?

00:17:55.410 --> 00:17:59.000
It's hard to say... We do pretty much anything.

00:17:59.000 --> 00:18:00.250
--Selecting CDs from the CD storage,

00:18:00.250 --> 00:18:01.450
--Oh, don't worry about it.
--Selecting CDs from the CD storage,

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:04.250
delivering faxes and compiling requests...

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:08.040
I did notice all those fax machines laying
around. Are they being used at all?

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.500
We never use them to send things out.

00:18:11.500 --> 00:18:15.790
But our older listeners still prefer
to send in their requests by fax.

00:18:15.790 --> 00:18:19.410
Those fax machines won't be
going anywhere for a while.

00:18:19.410 --> 00:18:26.000
I still remember how impressed I was with their
new equipment when I first arrived at MRS.

00:18:26.000 --> 00:18:29.750
It was a shock compared to the community radio
station I used to volunteer at as a student.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:33.660
Their facility was more like
a high school radio club room.

00:18:33.660 --> 00:18:34.830
Wow, I see.

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:39.620
But what I love about radio is how
you can still make things happen,

00:18:39.620 --> 00:18:42.620
even if the equipment is from ancient times.

00:18:45.330 --> 00:18:47.000
Huh? What's up?

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:50.540
Oh, I just remembered something funny.

00:18:50.540 --> 00:18:51.870
"She got tipsy before me?"
What?

00:18:51.870 --> 00:18:56.830
Remember what Mr. Mato said to you
when you first came to MRS?

00:18:56.830 --> 00:18:59.580
In radio, we have the three-second rule.

00:18:59.580 --> 00:19:04.950
Three seconds of silence is a gaffe;
eight seconds of silence will get me canned.

00:19:04.950 --> 00:19:09.000
If you're going to stop it,
make it worth your while.

00:19:09.000 --> 00:19:11.250
He over-exaggerated, big time.

00:19:11.250 --> 00:19:13.160
What?! Are you serious?

00:19:13.160 --> 00:19:15.540
While it's true that abrupt silence is bad,

00:19:15.540 --> 00:19:20.540
if there was eight seconds of silence, at most
we'd probably just have a meeting about it.

00:19:20.540 --> 00:19:21.870
A meeting?!

00:19:21.870 --> 00:19:23.870
What is this? School?

00:19:23.870 --> 00:19:25.500
You all are so soft.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:30.540
Another good thing about radio is how
listeners are generally very positive.

00:19:30.540 --> 00:19:34.870
Even if a host makes a blunder,
we rarely get any complaints.

00:19:34.870 --> 00:19:37.000
Rather, we get messages of encouragement!

00:19:37.000 --> 00:19:38.950
You guys are spoiled by the listeners.

00:19:38.950 --> 00:19:40.830
You're also being really blunt right now.

00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:45.330
That's why you guys have the gall to let
an amateur improvise on air by herself.

00:19:45.330 --> 00:19:47.620
Aren't you aware of the risks?

00:19:47.620 --> 00:19:50.500
But that was so entertaining!

00:19:50.500 --> 00:19:52.290
The listeners loved it, too.

00:19:52.290 --> 00:19:53.580
That's not the point!

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:54.870
All right! I've decided!

00:19:54.870 --> 00:19:59.700
In order to reform your thinking, I'll be
the first in the history of Moiwayama Radio...

00:19:59.700 --> 00:20:02.790
...to cause destruction
with listener's complaints!

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:09.660
She's rolling on the floor when I didn't
even say anything that funny.

00:20:09.660 --> 00:20:11.450
She laughs too easy.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:22.950
Come to think of it...
You're working tomorrow, too, right?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:24.540
Jeez, I'm sorry.

00:20:24.540 --> 00:20:27.200
For being an unemployed drunk.

00:20:27.200 --> 00:20:29.910
I'm the worst, aren't I?

00:20:29.910 --> 00:20:33.040
I had so much fun today.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:36.290
I've been wanting to talk to you, Miss Minare.

00:20:36.290 --> 00:20:38.330
What? Why?

00:20:38.330 --> 00:20:42.540
You left a strong impression on me that day.

00:20:42.540 --> 00:20:49.250
I felt like you were vocalizing
the thoughts I have in my head.

00:20:49.250 --> 00:20:51.950
"I will kill you even If I have to chase you
down to the end of the earth!"

00:20:51.950 --> 00:20:54.700
I want to do that, too!

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.120
By that you mean, you want to say it, too.

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.750
Ah, yes. You're right.

00:20:59.750 --> 00:21:03.580
But to tell you the truth, I've never
had a boyfriend before.

00:21:03.580 --> 00:21:06.660
So I probably don't fully understand
where you're coming from.

00:21:06.660 --> 00:21:08.910
Oh, don't you worry about that.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:11.750
Men are worthless, trust me.

00:21:11.750 --> 00:21:13.450
Not that I'm any better.

00:21:13.450 --> 00:21:15.750
There's no rush to have a boyfriend.

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.950
Mizuho, I suggest you stay a virgin forever.

00:21:17.950 --> 00:21:21.250
I'm sorry... forever is a bit much...

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:25.040
I feel like a classmate
once told me the same thing.

00:21:25.040 --> 00:21:26.700
Ah! Oh, yeah!

00:21:27.700 --> 00:21:29.160
Now's the time to tune in!

00:21:29.160 --> 00:21:30.000
Huh?

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:36.450
♪ MRS... JOZV FM. ♪

00:21:36.450 --> 00:21:39.950
Ah, so this is Sound High Tide.

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:42.830
They play songs non-stop until
the morning without any commentary.

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:47.160
They play the jingle once every
ten minutes, but yes, you're right.

00:21:47.160 --> 00:21:52.160
When you leave it on at low volume,
it helps you sleep better than total silence.

00:21:54.950 --> 00:21:56.620
Good night.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:22:00.540
♪ Moiwayama Radio Station. ♪

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:05.160
JOZV FM, this is Moiwayama Radio.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:09.750
Even the radio's assistant director
is asleep at 3:30 AM.

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:14.040
Hello, how is everyone doing?
This is Minare Koda.

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:44.750
"Next Episode"

00:23:44.750 --> 00:23:45.700
"Next Episode"
Miss Minare, I'm going to be direct.

00:23:45.700 --> 00:23:46.620
"Preview"
Miss Minare, I'm going to be direct.

00:23:46.620 --> 00:23:51.410
"Preview"
I didn't fall for a gullible woman who
gets lured into doing risky business.

00:23:51.410 --> 00:23:52.790
"Preview"
--Take that!
--Ouch!

00:23:52.790 --> 00:23:55.540
"Preview"
Nakahara! I'm about to punch you right now!

00:23:55.540 --> 00:24:00.080
"Preview"
I'll keep punching you,
and I won't admit that you're right!

00:24:00.080 --> 00:24:01.500
"Preview"
You already punched me.

00:24:01.500 --> 00:24:04.040
"Preview"
Is this Mr. Yoshiki Takarada's restaurant?

00:24:04.040 --> 00:24:05.540
"Preview"
Oh, yes. This is it.

00:24:05.540 --> 00:24:06.910
"Preview"
I'd like to sincerely apologize...

00:24:06.910 --> 00:24:08.330
"Preview"
Uh, who are you?

00:24:08.330 --> 00:24:10.500
"Preview"
A new character stirs up a storm!

00:24:10.500 --> 00:24:14.000
Next, on <i>Wave, Listen to Me!</i>: "You Don't Smile."

00:24:14.000 --> 00:24:16.950
"See you next time!"
"Illustrated by Hiroaki Samura"
